// The costume room's treasure chest: OSRS's costume storage, for treasure trail reward items.
//
// THE LIST IS DERIVED, NOT REMEMBERED. Every obj below appears in one of the three clue reward
// tables - scripts/minigames/game_trail/scripts/*/trail_clue_*_reward.rs2 - and every one of them
// is a clue VARIANT rather than something a shop sells: the god, gold-trimmed, trimmed and
// heraldic armour by name, plus the costume pieces clues are the only source of. Battery group 55
// re-derives that set from the reward tables on every run, so a clue reward added later that
// belongs in the chest cannot be quietly left out of it.
//
// The plain rune, adamant and black armour that clues also drop is deliberately NOT here, and
// neither are the bows, plain dragonhide, plain studded leather, amulets, coins, runes or noted
// fish. The chest is costume storage, not a second bank.
//
// 96 items in 20 sets. They are stored in SET ORDER and the first/last tables below are what make
// a set addressable without an enum per set - the same idiom poh_fam_first/poh_fam_last uses for
// the furniture families.
//
// GREW FROM 72 TO 96 ON 2026-10-15, because the hard rare table grew from 34 rows to Old School's
// own 158 on 2026-10-04 and the chest was not re-derived after it. What came in:
//   nine plateskirts, one per plate set - the chest held every set's helm, body, legs and shield
//     and not one of its skirts
//   the blue wizard robe skirt, trimmed and gold, beside the top that was already here
//   green and blue dragonhide, trimmed and gold - the trims are clue-only, which is why they
//     belong here while the plain hide does not
//   studded body and chaps (g), same rule
//   the three rune scimitar ornament kits
//
// AND THE FIFTEEN HERALDIC SHIELDS ARE THE IMPORT'S, not the cache's. This build has them twice:
// the 377 cache's rune/adamant/black_heraldic_kiteshield1..5, and *_shield_h1..h5 imported with
// Old School's 510 on 2026-10-04. Neither record carries a param or a gate the other lacks, so
// the tie breaks on the only thing that matters to a chest: the import's fifteen are what the
// clue tables hand out and what the collection log tracks, and the cache's fifteen are what
// nothing gives any more. Fifteen slots that could never be filled are now fifteen that can. The
// cache's fifteen are named in tools/nosourcespec.json for the same reason the duplicate magic
// secateurs are.

[poh_costume_item]
inputtype=int
outputtype=namedobj
default=null
val=0,rune_full_helm_saradomin
val=1,rune_platebody_saradomin
val=2,rune_platelegs_saradomin
val=3,rune_plateskirt_saradomin
